This question tests end-to-end thinking for a real-time AWS ML workflow with PrivateLink, including model choice, training strategy, endpoint sizing, canary rollout, and monitoring for drift and privacy. Key concepts covered include SageMaker training with transfer learning on image-caption data, PrivateLink access to a VPC-hosted endpoint, real-time endpoint autoscaling and latency targeting, canary rollout and rollback criteria, and Model Monitor for drift and privacy checks.

```javascript
// Training config
const config = {
  encoder: 'EfficientNet-Lite0',
  decoder: 'TransformerDecoder',
  vocabularySize: 8000,
  augmentation: ['random_crop', 'horizontal_flip', 'color_jitter'],
  learningRate: 0.001,
  batchSize: 32,
  epochs: 20
};

// Endpoint config
const endpointConfig = {
  instanceType: 'ml.g4dn.xlarge',
  minInstances: 1,
  maxInstances: 3,
  scalingTarget: { metric: 'P99Latency', value: 500 },
  cooldown: 300
};

// Canary rollout
const canaryConfig = {
  initialTraffic: 5,
  stages: [5, 25, 50, 100],
  stageDuration: 86400,
  rollback: { latencyThreshold: 600, errorRateThreshold: 0.01 }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience building production ML pipelines in AWS with strict data locality, latency targets, and privacy. Assesses ability to combine PrivateLink, Lake Formation, Feature Store, canary deployment, drift monitoring, and cost governance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker PrivateLink
- Lake Formation data access
- Feature Store
- Endpoint traffic splitting (canary)
- Drift detection & retraining triggers
- DP privacy controls and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example drift score calculation (KS statistic placeholder)
function ksDrift(p, q) {
  let max = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < p.length; i++) {
    max = Math.max(max, Math.abs(p[i] - q[i]));
  }
  return max;
}
```

